--   Brownian motion relative to a filtration
-- statement:
--   Vendored from LevyStochCalc, repository https://github.com/cgarryZA/LevyStochCalc, commit 984dbf0b790031eac05d56fe5a84b65e15e1e932. `IsBrownianFiltration W ℱ` requires that every W t is measurable with respect to ℱ t and that, for each 0 ≤ s, ℱ s is independent of the supremum σ-algebra generated by all increments W t − W s with t > s. The theorem `IsBrownianFiltration.indep` derives independence for one increment, and `stronglyMeasurable` gives strong measurability of each time slice. The conditional-expectation results state that an increment after s has conditional expectation zero and that, for 0 ≤ s ≤ t, the conditional expectation of W t given ℱ s equals W s almost everywhere.
